  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 103.39 Marsh",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 103.39 “Marsh” means a wetland that is distinguished by soft-stemmed herbaceous plants such as grasses, rushes, and sedges, where the water table is at or above the surface throughout the year but can fluctuate seasonally, as determined using the federal classification method. The term includes freshwater marshes and tidal marshes.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 103.37)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt100.html"
